Package: fotobox-print-bridge
Version: 0.1.0
Architecture: any
Maintainer: Fotobox
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends: cups-daemon (>= 2.2), cups-filters, printer-driver-gutenprint (>= 5.3), avahi-daemon, passwd, libcups2 (>= 2.2) | libcups2t64
Recommends: qrencode
Description: Fotobox print bridge: USB dye-sub printing for the Fotobox app over the LAN
 Turns a small Linux box (Raspberry Pi, any Debian/Ubuntu machine) into the
 CUPS print host for Fotobox booths: plug a DNP or Citizen dye-sub printer in
 by USB and the booth app prints to it over the local network, no jailbreak
 needed. Uses the distribution's CUPS and Gutenprint; adds the queue manager
 (one queue per attached printer, default page size from the loaded paper),
 a LAN-only, token-protected cupsd configuration and DNS-SD discovery.
